        "id": 117890,
        "name": "Rabit",
        "username": "Rabit",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/{size}/7330_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-01-01T14:14:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Pydro\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pydro/48/1844_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Pydro:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>OK, here is my suggestion for the video game (yes, I know it will be a pain to code):One of my favorite little surprises in SotM is when the effect matches the art on the card. When this happens, a little pop up of \"Art Match!\" should come up.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Heh, actually that wouldn't so much be a pain to code (from my experience - but I don't know anything about Unity, which this is developed with), as a pain to go back and enter data for all the cards so the game would know it's an art match.  <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/wink.png?v=12\" title=\":wink:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":wink:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>",
